  </p>
  <p>
    The contract language is English. Mandatory Spanish and EU consumer rules
    still apply where you qualify as a consumer or user under Royal
    Legislative Decree 1/2007 (TRLGDCU).
  </p>

  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    Zenguy provides automated browser testing from natural-language
    instructions, HTTP uptime monitoring, incident records, evidence
    (including screenshots and Markdown reports), and notifications. Results
    may contain false positives, false negatives, delays or incomplete
    information. Zenguy is an operational aid. It is not a substitute for your
    own security, backup, QA, compliance or business-continuity controls, and
    it does not guarantee that your site will keep working.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Accounts</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least 18 and provide accurate information. You must protect
    credentials and secrets and tell us promptly if you suspect misuse. One
    person must not share a login; invite teammates to the workspace instead.
    We may refuse, suspend or close an account for a material breach, unlawful
    or dangerous use, a security risk, non-payment, or when the law requires
    it. Where practical we will give notice and a chance to fix the issue.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may close the account from the product settings or by emailing{" "}
    <a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a>. Evidence follows the
    30-day retention in the Privacy Policy; billing records may be kept longer
    where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    You may test only sites, accounts and systems you own or are authorised to
    access. You must not use Zenguy to attack, overload, evade security
    controls, scrape unlawfully, distribute malware, violate privacy, infringe
    rights, or break any law. You must not probe Zenguy itself, our
    infrastructure, or other customers.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Customer content and processor terms</h2>
  <p>
    You keep ownership of the configurations, instructions, secrets and other
    content you submit. You grant us a limited licence to host, process,
    transmit and display that content solely to operate Zenguy.
  </p>
  <p>
    When that content includes personal data of third parties, you are the
    controller and {legalCompany.legalName} is the processor (art. 28 GDPR).
    In that role we will:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>process the data only on your documented instructions (the configuration you save and the runs you request);</li>
    <li>ensure persons authorised to process it are bound by confidentiality;</li>
    <li>use the technical and organisational measures described in the Privacy Policy;</li>
    <li>use the subprocessors listed there, and tell you of material changes;</li>
    <li>help you answer data-subject requests, so far as the product allows;</li>
    <li>notify you without undue delay after becoming aware of a personal-data breach affecting data we process for you;</li>
    <li>delete run evidence on the 30-day cycle, and other processor data when you delete the workspace, except data we must keep as controller (billing, security);</li>
    <li>make available information reasonably needed to show these obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You are responsible for the legality of the content, for avoiding
    unnecessary production personal data in tests, and for backups of anything
    you still need after our retention window.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Notifications and SMS</h2>
  <p>
    You must have each recipient’s permission before adding an email, phone,
    WhatsApp or other destination. Zenguy SMS is a recurring operational-alert
    programme for requested test failures, downtime, recoveries and channel
    verification. Frequency follows monitoring activity and may include
    several messages in a day. Message and data rates may apply. Carriers are
    not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.
  </p>
  <p>
    Recipients may reply STOP to opt out of SMS from the sending number, or
    HELP for help, or you can remove the channel in Zenguy. Consent to SMS is
    not a condition of purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Fees, taxes and cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    Paid plans, included runs, overage, prepaid alert credit, taxes, the
    billing cycle and renewal are shown before you pay and require your
    express agreement (LSSI-CE arts. 27 and 28; TRLGDCU). Checkout is hosted
    by Stripe. Subscriptions renew until cancelled; cancellation takes effect
    at the end of the period already paid, as shown in the billing portal,
    unless a mandatory rule says otherwise.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prices on marketing pages are a reference. The binding price is the one
    Stripe shows, with applicable VAT or equivalent tax. SMS, voice and
    WhatsApp alerts are charged per alert from prepaid credit at the
    destination prices shown in the product. Credit is only spent on alerts
    you configure, never goes negative, and is returned when a carrier rejects
    a message.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a consumer, EU cooling-off rules for digital services apply
    (TRLGDCU and Directive 2011/83/EU, as amended). Because Zenguy starts as
